# vapi — container for the Millie voice control plane

Runtime image for `~/work/projects/droyfun/millie` (ADR-0005: Millie has no
host Python; everything runs in here).

Vapi itself is a hosted HTTP service at api.vapi.ai — there is no Vapi server
to run locally and no official Vapi image. This container holds *our* client
side: Python + uv + millie's dependencies. Millie talks to Vapi over HTTPS
with httpx; the Vapi Python SDK is deliberately not used (millie ADR-0003).

## Build

The Dockerfile installs millie's dependencies from millie's own
`pyproject.toml`, so **the build context is the millie repo, not this
directory**:

    ./build.sh                     # uses the default millie path
    ./build.sh /path/to/millie     # or point it somewhere else

Equivalent to:

    docker build -f Dockerfile -t millie-dev /path/to/millie

One source of truth for dependencies (millie's `pyproject.toml`); the image
definition lives here with the other AI tool sandboxes.

## Use

From the millie repo — the launcher builds on demand and mounts the narrow
write surface:

    bin/millie doctor
    bin/millie shell

`dev_container.sh` is the central-builder script, kept here for parity with
the other `ai/*` sandboxes; millie's own `make buildsh` uses the copy in
`~/work/projects/builder/`.
